  "description": "Issue #18 sprint 4 core semantic milestone: the blocking first-start selector actually appears on a real multi-locale (EXPANSION_ENABLED_LOCALES=en,qps-ploc EXPANSION_PSEUDO_LOCALE=1) debug ROM booted from a real ExpansionUserPrefs UNSET fixture (active=1 at frame 600/660, no stray input given -- only the health/safety/Nintendo/IS skip presses, deliberately NOT the longer generic intro-mash recipe other scenarios use, since the selector opens much earlier than those and a stray A/START would otherwise be consumed as an immediate 'confirm row 0' before this scenario's own DOWN+A gets to run), then DOWN (move cursor to the qps-ploc row) + A (confirm) actually dismisses it (active 1->0) and commits the selection: selectedLocale AND currentLocale both become 0x07 (qps-ploc), cacheGeneration goes 0->1. currentLocale tracking selectedLocale is itself the empirical, real-capture proof that this sprint's critical fix (sCurrentLocale/sCacheLocale/sCacheMsgId were missing EWRAM_DATA, silently placing them in the read-only ROM output section per linker/expansion.ld, making ExpansionLocale_SetCurrent() a complete no-op) actually restores real locale-switching behavior -- before the fix, currentLocale would have stayed 0x00 here forever regardless of selection. See docs/localization.md's 'Runtime placement pitfall' section.",
